  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through next Thursday) \nIssued at 1046 AM CDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nThe last wave of showers will come Saturday night into Sunday with \nan additional push of upper level energy. This will also shove the \nboundary farther south putting an end to the rain chances by the end \nof Sunday night. Rainfall totals have not changed much with this \nforecast cycle with a medium to high chance of picking up at least \nhalf an inch and a medium chance of picking up at least one inch. \nWhile the rain is welcomed, it will not do much in the way of \nrelieving the drought across the area. Today's new drought monitor \nshows an expansion of the D2 (moderate drought) and D3 (severe \ndrought) across western and middle Tennessee. Unfortunately, after \nthe weekend rain, the pattern once again turns dry next week with no \nappreciable rain chances through the work week. Temperatures will be \ncloser to normal next week with lows in the 40s and 50s and highs in \nthe 70s. High temperatures may creep up into the 80s by mid week.",
